for the goofballs, sweetheart.

277
00:19:08,564 --> 00:19:09,857
Let's fix yours next.

278
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,192
The ones for your bridesmaids
and maid of honor.

279
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:24,121
The world really is a small place, huh?

280
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:27,708
Who would've thought your Mama Yaya

281
00:19:27,791 --> 00:19:29,001
would turn out to be Rahmboy's mother?

282
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:34,131
Even I was surprised.

283
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,719
By the way, sweetheart.

284
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:43,307
How come you never told me
about your Mama Yaya?

285
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:50,397
Well, it just slipped my mind, sweetheart.

286
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:52,399
And besides, you know,

287
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:55,903
a lot of things happened
between the two of us,

288
00:19:55,986 --> 00:20:01,366
and to be honest, I just
never thought we'd see each other again.

289
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,537
I'm glad you found each other again.

290
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:07,831
Right?

291
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:13,003
Ow.

292
00:20:13,086 --> 00:20:14,129
Ouch!

293
00:20:15,422 --> 00:20:16,840
- Sweetheart, I'm sorry.
- Ow.

294
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:17,966
I thought there was, you know,

295
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:19,593
an insect.

296
00:20:19,676 --> 00:20:20,886
- I thought there was a bug.
- A bug?

297
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:22,804
I saw it. There it is.

298
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:26,892
I thought you were starting to miss
your violent life.

299
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:27,935
That hurts!

300
00:20:30,812 --> 00:20:32,522
I'd never miss that.

301
00:20:32,606 --> 00:20:35,317
Really? My side seems
to be telling me otherwise.

302
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,365
I'm just joking, sweetheart.

303
00:20:42,074 --> 00:20:45,494
Of course, I know you're not
going back to that life.

304
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:50,832
I know. This is where we belong.

305
00:20:52,417 --> 00:20:54,378
Living the quiet life
we've always dreamed of.

306
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:55,963
Right?

307
00:21:01,468 --> 00:21:02,719
Don't stress about it, okay?

308
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,024
So playful.

309
00:22:17,210 --> 00:22:19,463
<i>So this is what having a family</i>
<i>feels like.</i>

310
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:21,757
<i>If only I could,</i>

311
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:25,010
<i>I'd want things to stay this way.</i>

312
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:27,637
<i>Being with them.</i>

313
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:11,908
<i>And I will end anyone,</i>

314
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:16,955
<i>anyone who tries to disrupt</i>
<i>our lives again.</i>

315
00:24:33,305 --> 00:24:34,806
Concordat.

316
00:24:53,950 --> 00:24:54,910
Are you ready?

317
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:56,620
I hope so.

318
00:24:57,287 --> 00:25:00,916
Let's hope Viktor and Donabel
make it here.

319
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:04,419
Did you hear?

320
00:25:04,502 --> 00:25:06,379
About ma'am's husband?

321
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:07,464
The one who used to be here.

322
00:25:07,547 --> 00:25:09,216
Viktor Valtrovi.

323
00:25:09,299 --> 00:25:10,717
Yes. It's pretty bad.

324
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:11,676
He's so beated.

325
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:13,553
What happened? Was there a riot?

326
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:15,639
All I heard was
that he could barely stand.

327
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:17,015
We're screwed.

328
00:25:17,098 --> 00:25:19,100
General Norberto might find out.

329
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:23,730
It's still unclear.

330
00:25:25,398 --> 00:25:28,068
We still don't know if there was a rumble

331
00:25:28,151 --> 00:25:30,070
or if he violated any rules in there.

332
00:25:30,153 --> 00:25:33,323
Maybe we can talk to General Norberto?

333
00:25:35,033 --> 00:25:36,368
There's an update.

334
00:25:38,453 --> 00:25:42,123
Once our dreams finally come true.

335
00:25:45,252 --> 00:25:48,046
I've found a new dream for myself.

336
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:50,423
I've built a new life that I want.

337
00:25:50,507 --> 00:25:52,425
I held up my end, Chiara.

338
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:54,636
It's time for you to hold up yours.
